# Privacy Policy — Polymarket Wallet Tracker

**Last updated:** October 9, 2026

Polymarket Wallet Tracker is a Chrome extension that monitors public trading activity from user-selected Polymarket wallets and provides notifications when configured trade conditions are met.

## Information We Access

The extension accesses public wallet addresses and publicly available trading activity from Polymarket's APIs to provide wallet monitoring and trade notifications.

Wallet addresses selected by users, monitoring preferences, notification thresholds, and locally stored trade history are stored in the user's browser.

## How Information Is Used

Information is used exclusively to provide the extension's features, including wallet tracking, trade detection, notification delivery, and local activity history.

## Data Sharing and Collection

The extension does not sell personal information or use tracked wallet activity for advertising.

The extension does not require Polymarket account credentials, private keys, seed phrases, or trading permissions.

Wallet monitoring requests are sent to Polymarket's public API services. Those services may receive technical information associated with API requests, subject to their own privacy practices.

The extension does not transmit locally stored watchlists or activity history to a developer-operated server unless a future version explicitly introduces such functionality and updates this policy accordingly.

## Data Storage and Retention

Wallet preferences and activity history are stored locally in Chrome. Users can remove tracked wallets or clear locally stored activity through the extension.

Uninstalling the extension may remove its locally stored data.

## Security

The extension uses reasonable technical measures to limit access to stored information and requests only the permissions necessary for its functionality.

## Changes to This Policy

This policy may be updated when the extension's functionality or data practices change. The latest version will be published at the same URL.

